cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "thermal-horizon-rar: Testing the Thermal-Horizon Reading of the Radial Acceleration Relation, from Galaxies to Wide Binaries"
version: "v1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Hájek"
    given-names: "Filip"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheCake/thermal-horizon-rar"
url: "https://github.com/TheCake/thermal-horizon-rar"
abstract: >-
  Measurement and theory-testing program for gravity at low accelerations, deposited
  as a complete repository snapshot: coefficient-level tests of the radial acceleration
  relation on SPARC rotation curves and KiDS-1000 lensing data; a joint two-dimensional
  (velocity, direction-angle) likelihood measurement of the low-acceleration velocity
  boost in 14,071 Gaia EDR3 wide binaries, with completeness marginalization, seed and
  bootstrap error budgets, and a noise-ceiling profile; the solar-system quadrupole
  consequences of the measured amplitude; a modified-inertia versus modified-gravity
  discrimination on the binary data; a reconciliation by ablation of the conflicting
  published wide-binary analyses; and a horizon-thermal mechanism programme with its
  exact results, its exclusions, and its open constants. Three manuscripts are under
  papers/ (wide binaries; radial-acceleration-relation coefficients; mechanism). The
  frozen internal record is PAPER.md; the chronological lab notebook, including every
  correction and retraction, is NOTES-horizon-inertia.md; the curated measurement
  ledger is LEDGER.csv; signed predictions registered before test are in
  PREDICTIONS.md. Every claimed number is reproduced by a named script under calcs/,
  and every analysis stage was pre-registered in a commit made before the run.
keywords:
  - MOND
  - radial acceleration relation
  - wide binaries
  - Gaia
  - SPARC
  - modified gravity
  - modified inertia
  - external field effect
  - galactic dynamics
  - de Sitter horizon thermodynamics
  - reproducible research
  - pre-registration
